## Consumer harness Python (`python-client/`)

Dois sockets:

| Socket | Papel |
|--------|--------|
| **:9750** | REG!, CRDY, PRDY, HBRP, ASGN, DELV, FAIL (control) |
| **:976x** | Listener BATC keep-alive (`serve_batch_on_connection`) |

- **fetch/process** desacoplados (`prefetch_batch_count`)
- **`accept_batch`**: janela por ciclo CRDY; fora da janela → drop silencioso + `stale_batches`
- **`batch_timeout_secs`**: default 10s; stress usa **12s** (&gt; producer delivery 8s)
- **`data_idle_secs`**: default **60s** — fecha TCP data se sem BATC (keep-alive idle)
- Chaos reconnect opcional

---

## Ring (`src/ring/`)

Usado no **producer local** (`ByteRing`, `BatchAccumulator`). Cap → **drop oldest**. **`SharedRing`** existe na lib mas **master atual não usa ring central** — backlog agregado vem dos heartbeats dos producers (`producer_backlog_*` em metrics).

